A CSS rule whose block never closes swallows the rest of the file: tree-sitter puts the unclosed
rule and every rule after it, the `@media` block's included, in one `ERROR` node, so only the
rule before it is listed (techdebt.md, "Declarations inside syntax errors are dropped").
== args
input/broken.css
== file input/broken.css
/* Styles. */
.before { color: red; }
.broken { color: blue;
.inner { margin: 0; }
@media print {
  .x { color: black; }
.after { color: green; }
== stdout
input/broken.css (7 lines)
Styles.
[L2-L2] .before
== stderr
== exit 0
